<title>GERMANY: BMW denies report it might sell Rover unit.</title>
<headline>BMW denies report it might sell Rover unit.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayerische Motoren Werke AG (BMW) strongly denied a press report it was considering selling the small car unit of its Rover Group to Chrysler Corp.</p>
<p>The Times newspaper reported in its Tuesday edition that Chrysler was trying to buy Rover's small car division including the Mini and Metro.</p>
<p>A BMW spokesman called the report &quot;complete nonsense&quot; and a fabrication.</p>
<p>The report said the Chrysler executives had inspected Rover production facilities with the consent of Rover.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
